select id, 'KOJOH-SBN-LIC-0011', 'standard', $pack${"phases": [{"key": "python", "title": "Phase 1, Python: Clean and Join the Data", "tasks": [{"id": "P2", "text": "Resolve PO revisions. Map every `Order_No` (`260411`, `260411.R`, `260411.R.1`) to its base PO, keep only the latest revision's lines, and keep the original PO date separately from each revision date. State how much the total ordered value would be overstated if you summed every revision."}, {"id": "P5", "text": "Standardise supplier names (each factory appears under up to seven spellings), ports (`TKD`, `ICD TKD`, `INTKD6`, `Tughlakabad` are one place; `ANY PORT IN INDIA` needs a decision), event names (16 standard events from about 60 spellings), document types (14 from about 45) and payment milestones (10 from about 30)."}, {"id": "P6", "text": "Split `Contact_Details` into contact name, email and phone where present. Parse `Containers` (`2 x 40HC + 1 x 20`, `2x40HC`, `2X40`, `3`) into a container count and a type mix. Parse `Order_Qty` (`1,200 pcs`) and `Advance_%` (`10%`, `10`, `0.10`, `NA`)."}, {"id": "P3", "text": "Write one money parser for USD and INR text (`$1,250.00`, `USD 1,250.00`, `US$1250`, `Rs 1,25,000`, `₹1,25,000`, `INR 125,000`, padded and `.00` forms) and normalise `Currency` (`usd`, `$`, `US$`, `Rs`, `₹`, blank). Find the instalments where one milestone was paid in two parts and make sure they add up."}, {"id": "P7", "text": "Clean `Container_No` (`MSKU 1234567`, `msku1234567`, `MSKU-1234567`), map events with a blank or `PO#` style reference back to their PO through the container or BL number, and de-duplicate events that more than one source reported, using the source priority in the definitions. Report how many duplicates you removed."}, {"id": "P4", "text": "Write one date parser for every date and timestamp column across the files: day first dates, `14-Mar-26`, ISO dates, ISO timestamps, `14/03/2026 6:42 PM` and Excel serial numbers. Event timestamps keep only the date."}, {"id": "P1", "text": "Load all six files and profile each one: rows, columns, nulls, and the keys that are meant to join them. Write down the five problems that would break a join or a sum if you ignored them."}, {"id": "P8", "text": "Build an `as_of(report_date)` function that returns the world as it looked on any date: POs that existed, the latest revision on that date, events that had happened, documents received and payments made. Every personal question in this pack runs through it, starting with your report date: **2 April 2026**."}]}, {"key": "sql", "title": "Phase 2, SQL: Answer the Business Questions", "tasks": [{"id": "S7", "text": "**Your transit tracker as of 2 April 2026:** every open PO with its stage, containers by stage, days since the last event, planned ETA and how late it is running. Then the totals: open POs and open containers by stage."}, {"id": "S2", "text": "Departure delay per supplier: days between Planned ETD and the PO's first Vessel Departed event. Rank the suppliers and show how many POs each figure rests on."}, {"id": "S9", "text": "**Payments as of 2 April 2026:** every unpaid instalment that is overdue, due in the next 14 days and due in 15 to 30 days, in its own currency and in rupees at the 2 April 2026 reference rate. Give the rupee total of each bucket."}, {"id": "S3", "text": "Sea transit days (Vessel Departed to Arrived at POD) by transshipment port (Colombo, Singapore, Port Klang, direct). How much does the slowest route cost in days against direct sailings?"}, {"id": "S6", "text": "Demurrage and detention paid, by supplier and by final destination. What share of the year's demurrage traces back to a single supplier, and what is the common cause?"}, {"id": "S5", "text": "Clearance time (arrival at the final destination to Out of Charge) for shipments where the Original BL / Telex Release and the BIS certificate were in hand before arrival, against shipments where they were not."}, {"id": "S1", "text": "Total ordered value (latest 