ry, in USD and as a share of the total. Which three suppliers carry the most spend?"}, {"id": "S4", "text": "Compare the PO register's `Revised_ETA` with the day each delivered PO actually reached its final destination. What share arrived more than 7 days later than the register said? Is the register a tracker or a wish list?"}, {"id": "S9", "text": "**Payments as of 11 April 2026:** every unpaid instalment that is overdue, due in the next 14 days and due in 15 to 30 days, in its own currency and in rupees at the 11 April 2026 reference rate. Give the rupee total of each bucket."}, {"id": "S7", "text": "**Your transit tracker as of 11 April 2026:** every open PO with its stage, containers by stage, days since the last event, planned ETA and how late it is running. Then the totals: open POs and open containers by stage."}, {"id": "S8", "text": "**Documents as of 11 April 2026:** list every document that is overdue, due in the next 14 days, and due in 15 to 30 days, with who owes it. Give the counts for each bucket and say which responsible party owes the most overdue documents."}, {"id": "S12", "text": "Landed cost per unit for every model with at least one delivered shipment: supplier cost + ocean freight + insurance + customs duty excluding IGST + CHA + demurrage + inland transport, allocated to lines by FOB value. Show the landed cost multiplier (landed rupees per rupee of FOB) by category."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: PO and Container Lookup", "tasks": [{"id": "D2", "text": "On the same page show that PO's documents checklist (received, pending, overdue, colour coded) and its payments schedule (paid, due, overdue) with rupee values."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a PO lookup: type a PO number (with or without `.R`) and see its latest revision lines, value, terms, supplier contact and every container with its stage and event timeline."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a container search: type a container or BL number and land on the right PO, with the full event history in date order and the source of each event."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add a report date control. Changing it must change every number on the page, so the page shows the world as it was on that day. Default it to 11 April 2026."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Add filters for supplier, final destination, stage and payment terms that work together (AND logic) with the report date."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Control Tower", "tasks": [{"id": "D11", "text": "A Revised ETA vs actual panel that shows how often the PO register is wrong and by how many days."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect the report date control and the supplier filter."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "A supplier scorecard: spend, departure delay, document lateness, demurrage caused and open POs, side by side so no single number decides who is a good supplier."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Control tower header: open POs, open containers by stage, documents overdue, payments overdue in rupees and LCs at risk, all as of the report date."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "An exchange rate panel: the USD/INR line with markers on every supplier payment, and the rupee cost of the rupee's fall across the year."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "A route panel: transit days by transshipment port and by destination, as distributions rather than averages."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "A focus page for your supplier, **Yuyao Mingtai Technology Co., Ltd.**: their open POs, containers on water, departure delay and overdue documents as of the report date."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "An 8 week cash requirement chart from the report date, stacked by payee type, with the overdue amount as its own bar."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "A landed cost panel by category and model, with the cost waterfall from FOB to landed rupees."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A documents ageing panel: overdue documents by responsible party and type, with the oldest called out by name."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short project write-up (Word, PDF, Notion or a README) with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you joined six messy files into one model, including revisions, event de-duplication and your as-of logic; (2) **Key Discoveries**: your top 3 to 5 findings, written for a head of supply chain; (3) **Recommendations**: at least 3 concrete, data-backed changes before the next festive season. Close with a one-page status note as of 11 April 2026: what is late, what documents to chase this week and what cash to arrange."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S3", "text": "Which routes should be avoided in August and September? Use rolled-over bookings and transit days."}, {"id": "X-S6", "text": "Compare FG and SKD orders on landed cost per unit after duty. Is SKD worth it, and for which categories?"}, {"id": "X-S4", "text": "Find POs where the warehouse has been waiting longest relative to plan and draft the escalation email you would send to each supplier."}]}], "brief": "**Your personal brief:** your report date is **11 April 2026** and your focus supplier is **Yuyao Mingtai Technology Co., Ltd.**. Treat 11 April 2026 as today: anything dated after it has not happened yet.", "premium": [{"id": "X3", "text": "**Audit the customs duty.** For each Bill of Entry, back out the BCD rate actually charged from the duty paid and the CIF value. Find the SKD shipments charged at the FG rate and work out the refund claim in rupees (BCD + SWS only)."}, {"id": "X2", "text": "**Predict the ETA.** Using only what was known at departure (supplier, route, port, month, rolled over or not), predict arrival at the final destination. Report the error against the PO register's Revised ETA."}, {"id": "X1", "text": "**Model it properly.** Design a normalised schema (supplier, product, PO, PO line with revisions, shipment, container, event, document, payment) and load it into a real SQL database. Rewrite S7 and S9 as single queries that take the report date as a parameter."}, {"id": "X5", "text": "**Supplier scorecard with weights.** Combine delay, document lateness, demurrage caused and price into one score, run a +/-10% sensitivity on each weight and say which suppliers stay in the top three."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Hedge or not.** If every supplier payment had been booked forward at the reference rate on the PO date, what would the company have saved or lost over the year? Show it by quarter."}]}$pack$::jsonb
