d? Is the register a tracker or a wish list?"}, {"id": "S8", "text": "**Documents as of 9 May 2026:** list every document that is overdue, due in the next 14 days, and due in 15 to 30 days, with who owes it. Give the counts for each bucket and say which responsible party owes the most overdue documents."}, {"id": "S10", "text": "**Cash plan from 9 May 2026:** rupees needed in each of the next 8 weeks (week 1 starts on 9 May 2026), split by payee type (supplier, freight, customs, CHA and the rest), with the overdue amount shown separately."}, {"id": "S6", "text": "Demurrage and detention paid, by supplier and by final destination. What share of the year's demurrage traces back to a single supplier, and what is the common cause?"}, {"id": "S1", "text": "Total ordered value (latest revisions, cancelled excluded) by supplier and by product category, in USD and as a share of the total. Which three suppliers carry the most spend?"}, {"id": "S3", "text": "Sea transit days (Vessel Departed to Arrived at POD) by transshipment port (Colombo, Singapore, Port Klang, direct). How much does the slowest route cost in days against direct sailings?"}, {"id": "S7", "text": "**Your transit tracker as of 9 May 2026:** every open PO with its stage, containers by stage, days since the last event, planned ETA and how late it is running. Then the totals: open POs and open containers by stage."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: PO and Container Lookup", "tasks": [{"id": "D1", "text": "Build a PO lookup: type a PO number (with or without `.R`) and see its latest revision lines, value, terms, supplier contact and every container with its stage and event timeline."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "On the same page show that PO's documents checklist (received, pending, overdue, colour coded) and its payments schedule (paid, due, overdue) with rupee values."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Add filters for supplier, final destination, stage and payment terms that work together (AND logic)