ngs), document types (14 from about 45) and payment milestones (10 from about 30)."}, {"id": "P4", "text": "Write one date parser for every date and timestamp column across the files: day first dates, `14-Mar-26`, ISO dates, ISO timestamps, `14/03/2026 6:42 PM` and Excel serial numbers. Event timestamps keep only the date."}, {"id": "P1", "text": "Load all six files and profile each one: rows, columns, nulls, and the keys that are meant to join them. Write down the five problems that would break a join or a sum if you ignored them."}]}, {"key": "sql", "title": "Phase 2, SQL: Answer the Business Questions", "tasks": [{"id": "S2", "text": "Departure delay per supplier: days between Planned ETD and the PO's first Vessel Departed event. Rank the suppliers and show how many POs each figure rests on."}, {"id": "S11", "text": "**LC risk as of 31 May 2026:** list the LCs at risk under the definition, with their last shipment date, how many containers are still to sail and the supplier."}, {"id": "S9", "text": "**Payments as of 31 May 2026:** every unpaid instalment that is overdue, due in the next 14 days and due in 15 to 30 days, in its own currency and in rupees at the 31 May 2026 reference rate. Give the rupee total of each bucket."}, {"id": "S7", "text": "**Your transit tracker as of 31 May 2026:** every open PO with its stage, containers by stage, days since the last event, planned ETA and how late it is running. Then the totals: open POs and open containers by stage."}, {"id": "S12", "text": "Landed cost per unit for every model with at least one delivered shipment: supplier cost + ocean freight + insurance + customs duty excluding IGST + CHA + demurrage + inland transport, allocated to lines by FOB value. Show the landed cost multiplier (landed rupees per rupee of FOB) by category."}, {"id": "S5", "text": "Clearance time (arrival at the final destination to Out of Charge) for shipments where the Original BL / Telex Release and the BIS certificate were in hand before arrival, against shipments where they were not."}, {"id": "S3", "text": "Sea transit days (Vessel Departed to Arrived at POD) by transshipment port (Colombo, Singapore, Port Klang, direct). How much does the slowest route cost in days against direct sailings?"}, {"id": "S10", "text": "**Cash plan from 31 May 2026:** rupees needed in each of the next 8 weeks (week 1 starts on 31 May 2026), split by payee type (supplier, freight, customs, CHA and the rest), with the overdue amount shown separately."}, {"id": "S8", "text": "**Documents as of 31 May 2026:** list every document that is overdue, due in the next 14 days, and due in 15 to 30 days, with who owes it. Give the counts for each bucket and say which responsible party owes the most overdue documents."}, {"id": "S6", "text": "Demurrage and detention paid, by supplier and by final destination. What share of the year's demurrage traces back to a single supplier, and what is the common cause?"}, {"id": "S4", "text": "Compare the PO register's `Revised_ETA` with the day each delivered PO actually reached its final destination. What share arrived more than 7 days later than the register said? Is the register a tracker or a wish list?"}, {"id": "S1", "text": "Total ordered value (latest revisions, cancelled excluded) by supplier and by product category, in USD and as a share of the total. Which three suppliers carry the most spend?"}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: PO and Container Lookup", "tasks": [{"id": "D3", "text": "Add a container search: type a container or BL number and land on the right PO, with the full event history in date order and the source of each event."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Add filters for supplier, final destination, stage and payment terms that work together (AND logic) with the report date."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "On the same page show that PO's documents checklist (received, pending, overdue, colour coded) and its payments schedule (paid, due, overdue) with rupee values."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a PO lookup: type a PO number (with or without `.R`) and see its latest revision lines, value, terms, supplier contact and every container with its stage and event timeline."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add a report date control. Changing it must change every number on the page, so the page shows the world as it was on that day. Default it to 31 May 2026."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Control Tower", "tasks": [{"id": "D11", "text": "A Revised ETA vs actual panel that shows how often the PO register is wrong and by how many days."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "An exchange rate panel: the USD/INR line with markers on every supplier payment, and the rupee cost of the rupee's fall across the year."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "A landed cost panel by category and model, with the cost waterfall from FOB to landed rupees."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect the report date control and the supplier filter."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "A supplier scorecard: spend, departure delay, document lateness, demurrage caused and open POs, side by side so no single number decides who is a good supplier."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "An 8 week cash requirement chart from the report date, stacked by payee type, with the overdue amount as its own bar."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A documents ageing panel: overdue documents by responsible party and type, with the oldest called out by name."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "A focus page for your supplier, **Ningbo Fenghe Electrical Appliance Co., Ltd.**: their open POs, containers on water, departure delay and overdue documents as of the report date."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "A route panel: transit days by transshipment port and by destination, as distributions rather than averages."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Control tower header: open POs, open containers by stage, documents overdue, payments overdue in rupees and LCs at risk, all as of the report date."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "ti