 11 June 2026."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a PO lookup: type a PO number (with or without `.R`) and see its latest revision lines, value, terms, supplier contact and every container with its stage and event timeline."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a container search: type a container or BL number and land on the right PO, with the full event history in date order and the source of each event."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Control Tower", "tasks": [{"id": "D6", "text": "Control tower header: open POs, open containers by stage, documents overdue, payments overdue in rupees and LCs at risk, all as of the report date."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "An 8 week cash requirement chart from the report date, stacked by payee type, with the overdue amount as its own bar."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "A route panel: transit days by transshipment port and by destination, as distributions rather than averages."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "A supplier scorecard: spend, departure delay, document lateness, demurrage caused and open POs, side by side so no single number decides who is a good supplier."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "A focus page for your supplier, **Shenzhen Xinyuda Technology Co., Ltd.**: their open POs, containers on water, departure delay and overdue documents as of the report date."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect the report date control and the supplier filter."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "A Revised ETA vs actual panel that shows how often the PO register is wrong and by how many days."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A documents ageing panel: overdue documents by responsible party and type, with the oldest called out by name."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "An exchange rate panel: the USD/INR line with markers on every supplier payment, and the rupee cost of the rupee's fall across the year."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "A landed cost panel by category and model, with the cost waterfall from FOB to landed rupees."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short project write-up (Word, PDF, Notion or a README) with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you joined six messy files into one model, including revisions, event de-duplication and your as-of logic; (2) **Key Discoveries**: your top 3 to 5 findings, written for a head of supply chain; (3) **Recommendations**: at least 3 concrete, data-backed changes before the next festive season. Close with a one-page status note as of 11 June 2026: what is late, what documents to chase this week and what cash to arrange."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S3", "text": "Which routes should be avoided in August and September? Use rolled-over bookings and transit days."}, {"id": "X-S4", "text": "Find POs where the warehouse has been waiting longest relative to plan and draft the escalation email you would send to each supplier."}, {"id": "X-S1", "text": "Recommend payment terms per supplier (advance %, credit days, TT or LC) using their delay and document record, and estimate the cash flow effect."}]}], "brief": "**Your personal brief:** your report date is **11 June 2026** and your focus supplier is **Shenzhen Xinyuda Technology Co., Ltd.**. Treat 11 June 2026 as today: anything dated after it has not happened yet.", "premium": [{"id": "X3", "text": "**Audit the customs duty.** For each Bill of Entry, back out the BCD rate actually charged from the duty paid and the CIF value. Find the SKD shipments charged at the FG rate and work out the refund claim in rupees (BCD + SWS only)."}, {"id": "X2", "text": "**Predict the ETA.** Using only what was known at departure (supplier, route, port, month, rolled over or not), predict arrival at the final destination. Report the error against the PO register's Revised ETA."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Hedge or not.** If every supplier payment had been booked forward at the reference rate on the PO date, what would the company have saved or lost over the year? Show it by quarter."}, {"id": "X1", "text": "**Model it properly.** Design a normalised schema (supplier, product, PO, PO line with revisions, shipment, container, event, document, payment) and load it into a real SQL database. Rewrite S7 and S9 as single queries that take the report date as a parameter."}, {"id": "X5", "text": "**Supplier scorecard with weights.** Combine delay, document lateness, demurrage caused and price into one score, run a +/-10% sensitivity on each weight and say which suppliers stay in the top three."}]}$pack$::jsonb
