select id, 'KOJOH-SBN-LIC-0092', 'standard', $pack${"phases": [{"key": "python", "title": "Phase 1, Python: Clean and Join the Data", "tasks": [{"id": "P3", "text": "Write one money parser for USD and INR text (`$1,250.00`, `USD 1,250.00`, `US$1250`, `Rs 1,25,000`, `₹1,25,000`, `INR 125,000`, padded and `.00` forms) and normalise `Currency` (`usd`, `$`, `US$`, `Rs`, `₹`, blank). Find the instalments where one milestone was paid in two parts and make sure they add up."}, {"id": "P1", "text": "Load all six files and profile each one: rows, columns, nulls, and the keys that are meant to join them. Write down the five problems that would break a join or a sum if you ignored them."}, {"id": "P4", "text": "Write one date parser for every date and timestamp column across the files: day first dates, `14-Mar-26`, ISO dates, ISO timestamps, `14/03/2026 6:42 PM` and Excel serial numbers. Event timestamps keep only the date."}, {"id": "P7", "text": "Clean `Container_No` (`MSKU 1234567`, `msku1234567`, `MSKU-1234567`), map events with a blank or `PO#` style reference back to their PO through the container or BL number, and de-duplicate events that more than one source reported, using the source priority in the definitions. Report how many duplicates you removed."}, {"id": "P5", "text": "Standardise supplier names (each factory appears under up to seven spellings), ports (`TKD`, `ICD TKD`, `INTKD6`, `Tughlakabad` are one place; `ANY PORT IN INDIA` needs a decision), event names (16 standard events from about 60 spellings), document types (14 from about 45) and payment milestones (10 from about 30)."}, {"id": "P6", "text": "Split `Contact_Details` into contact name, email and phone where present. Parse `Containers` (`2 x 40HC + 1 x 20`, `2x40HC`, `2X40`, `3`) into a container count and a type mix. Parse `Order_Qty` (`1,200 pcs`) and `Advance_%` (`10%`, `10`, `0.10`, `NA`)."}, {"id": "P8", "text": "Build an `as_of(report_date)` function that returns the world as it looked on any date: POs that existed, the latest revision on that date, events that had happened, documents received and payments made. Every personal question in this pack runs through it, starting with your report date: **22 June 2026**."}, {"id": "P2", "text": "Resolve PO revisions. Map every `Order_No` (`260411`, `260411.R`, `260411.R.1`) to its base PO, keep only the latest revision's lines, and keep the original PO date separately from each revision date. State how much the total ordered value would be overstated if you summed every revision."}]}, {"key": "sql", "title": "Phase 2, SQL: Answer the Business Questions", "tasks": [{"id": "S4", "text": "Compare the PO register's `Revised_ETA` with the day each delivered PO actually reached its final destination. What share arrived more than 7 days later than the register said? Is the register a tracker or a wish list?"}, {"id": "S1", "text": "Total ordered value (latest revisions, cancelled excluded) by supplier and by product category, in USD and as a share of the total. Which three suppliers carry the most spend?"}, {"id": "S3", "text": "Sea transit days (Vessel Departed to Arrived at POD) by transshipment port (Colombo, Singapore, Port Klang, direct). How much does the slowest route cost in days against direct sailings?"}, {"id": "S9", "text": "**Payments as of 22 June 2026:** every unpaid instalment that is overdue, due in the next 14 days and due in 15 to 30 days, in its own currency and in rupees at the 22 June 2026 reference rate. Give the rupee total of each bucket."}, {"id": "S7", "text": "**Your transit tracker as of 22 June 2026:** every open PO with its stage, containers by stage, days since the last event, planned ETA and how late it is running. Then the totals: open POs and open containers by stage."}, {"id": "S5", "text": "Clearance time (arrival at the final destination to Out of Charge) for shipments where the Original BL / Telex Release and the BIS certificate were in hand before arrival, against shipments where they were not."}, {"id": "S10", "text": "**Cash plan from 22 June 2026:** rupees needed in each of the next 8 weeks (week 1 starts on 22 June 2026), split by payee type (supplier, freight, customs, CHA and the rest), with the overdue amount shown separately."}, {"id": "S6", "text": "Demurrage and detention paid, by supplier and by final destination. What share of the year's demurrage traces back to a single supplier, and what is the common cause?"}, {"id": "S8", "text": "**Documents as of 22 June 2026:** list every document that is overdue, due in the next 14 days, and due in 15 to 30 days, with who owes it. Give the counts for each bucket and say which responsible party owes the most overdue documents."}, {"id": "S2", "text": "Departure delay per supplier: days between Planned ETD and the PO's first Vessel Departed event. Rank the suppliers and show how many POs each figure rests on."}, {"id": "S11", "text": "**LC risk as of 22 June 2026:** list the LCs at risk under the definition, with their last shipment date, how many containers are still to sail and the supplier."}, {"id": "S12", "text": "Landed cost per unit for every model with at least one delivered shipment: supplier cost + ocean freight + insurance + customs duty excluding IGST + CHA + demurrage + inland transport, allocated to lines by FOB value. Show the landed cost multiplier (landed rupees per rupee of FOB) by category."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: PO and Container Lookup", "tasks": [{"id": "D5", "text": "Add filters for supplier, final destination, stage and payment terms that work together (AND logic) with the report date."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add a report date control. Changing it must change every number on the page, so the page shows the world as it was on that day. Default it to 22 June 2026."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "On the same page show that PO's documents checklist (received, pending, overdue, colour coded) and its payments schedule (paid, due, overdue) with rupee values."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a PO lookup: type a PO number (with or without `.R`) and see its latest revision lines, value, terms, supplier contact and every container with its stage and event timeline."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a container search: type a container or BL number and land on the right PO, with the full event history in date order and the source of each event."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Control Tower", "tasks": [{"id": "D14", "text": "A focus page for your supplier, **Hangzhou Tianrun Garment Care Co., Ltd.**: their open POs, containers on water, departure delay and overdue documents as of the report date."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Control tower header: open POs, open containers by stage, documents overdue, payments overdue in rupees and LCs at risk, all as of the report date."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "A landed cost panel by category and model, with the cost waterfall from FOB to landed rupees."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "A route panel: transit days by transshipment port and by destination, as distributions rather than averages."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "A supplier scorecard: spend, departure delay, document lateness, demurrage caused and open POs, side by side so no single number decides who is a good supplier."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "An 8 week cash requirement chart from the report date, stacked by payee type, with the overdue amount as its own bar."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A documents ageing panel: overdue documents by responsible party and type, with the oldest called out by name."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "A Revised ETA vs actual panel that shows how often the PO register is wrong and by how many days."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect the report date control and the supplier filter."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "An exchange rate panel: the USD/INR line with markers on every supplier payment, and the rupee cost of the rupee's fall across the year."}]}, {"key": "documentation",